Z||000003||Borgio||11-02-2001||12:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiatic:<BR><B>i've been without my fiero for 2 days and am suffering from withdrawl.....must get tires!!!! well i can just dream the 3800 in the buick im driving is actually behind me and im going really fast. any other solutions to fiero withdrawl?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Me too, i've been with out my fieros for over 2 months. Its my stupid fault though. Went to college without taking one; reminds me I should be doing my homework. I didn't know how much I would miss it, i'm bringing it back after thanksgiving break. But my fieros have been running/licensed off and on for years now. I'm with Mach10, just sit in it, pretend, row through the gears, I've done it. There's nothing like driving one. On the upside, when you get back in it you'll feel GREAT! <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jake||||reg||1
